  "notes": "{捻|ねじ}る is a transitive verb ({他動詞|たどうし}). The intransitive form is {捻|ねじ}れる (to be twisted).\n\nASPECT ({ている}):\nThe ている form indicates ongoing action or a resulting state ({紐|ひも}が{捻|ねじ}れている = 'the rope is twisted').\n\nPARTICLE PATTERNS:\n- [object]を{捻|ねじ}る (twist ~)\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {腕|うで}を{捻|ねじ}る (twist someone's arm)\n- {蓋|ふた}を{捻|ねじ}る (twist a lid)\n- {首|くび}を{捻|ねじ}る (tilt one's head in thought)\n- {事実|じじつ}を{捻|ねじ}る (distort the facts)\n\nRELATED:\nThe noun ねじ (screw) comes from the same root. {首|くび}を{捻|ねじ}る is an idiom meaning to tilt one's head when puzzled or thinking.",
